<%# Sticky action drawer — peeks up from the bottom while the primary actions
    (#primary-actions) are scrolled out of view, so Save / Preview / (Un)publish
    + the save-state dot stay reachable in long content. Lives inside the editor
    controller so the buttons' actions and the saveDot/saveMessage targets
    resolve to it.

    translate-y-full = hidden by default; the editor-drawer controller adds the
    transition after the first paint so the on-load restore is instant (no slide
    flash on save/refresh).

    Locals: resource, resource_type. %>
<div data-controller="editor-drawer"
     data-editor-drawer-anchor-value="#primary-actions"
     class="fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-40 translate-y-full bg-white border-t border-gray-800 px-8 py-2 shadow-[0_-2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.08)] flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
  <%= render "shared/editor_primary_actions", resource: resource, resource_type: resource_type %>

  <%# FIND: the live editor's find-and-replace (⌘F), which opens just above
      this bar. Here rather than in the primary actions partial, so it isn't
      copied into the actions row at the top of the page. The markdown-editor
      controller finds it by data-roe-find-button, wires the click and
      unhides it once the live editor has loaded — this bar sits outside that
      controller's element, so a data-action couldn't reach it. %>
  <button type="button"
          data-roe-find-button
          title="Find and replace (⌘F)"
          class="hidden shrink-0 uppercase text-xs px-1.5 py-0 border border-gray-800 bg-gray-200 hover:bg-gray-300 font-mono rounded-xs h-4.5 leading-none pt-[0.1rem] cursor-pointer">Find</button>
</div>
